/**
 * Golden values of TFC's surface heights (M2-GEN-06). They come from TFC at c3b4d9536: an oracle compiled TFC's own
 * {@code ChunkHeightFiller}, {@code ChunkBiomeSampler}, {@code Kernel}, {@code BiomeNoiseSampler}, {@code BiomeNoise},
 * {@code BiomeBuilder}, {@code BiomeExtension}, the builder chains of {@code TFCBiomes}, {@code shore/*}, the river samplers,
 * the cinder cone sampler and {@code TFCLayers.createRegionBiomeLayer} with its layers, over TFC's region generator, with
 * Minecraft 1.21.11's {@code Mth} and fastutil. Stubs: no surface builders, the registry as a list, the volcano samplers
 * reduced to the cinder cones (the only one the plugin ports), and the chunk data generator's five seeds drawn in its place.
 * The column was sampled as {@code sampleHeight} does ({@code setupColumn}, {@code prepareColumnBiomeWeights},
 * {@code sampleColumnHeightAndBiome}) with {@code updateLocalCaches} reading the biome; {@code sampleAquiferSurfaceHeight} and
 * {@code sampleRiverDistSq} were copied from {@code ChunkNoiseFiller}. No server was started.
 *
 * <p>The chunks are the first chunk (on rings of 7-chunk steps around the origin, negative coordinates included) of up to 40
 * distinct biomes per seed, and the first 4 with a river biome. Each line holds a hash over the 256 integer heights and the
 * 256 biomes, the extremes, the 4 x 4 aquifer heights, and four sampled columns (final height, height before the cones,
 * biome). TFC sums the biome weights in the iteration order of an identity hash map, which changes with the JVM's hash
 * (the oracle's doubles moved with {@code -XX:hashCode=3}, its integers and biomes did not), so the doubles are compared
 * within 1e-4 and everything else exactly.
 */
